        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-30T16:20:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This global list of all dexpreopted files looks weird to me. Usually Soong doesn\u0027t know what goes into the system image because it\u0027s decided in the install stage in make. Is that different for the dexpreopted class paths?\n\nIsn\u0027t the \"real\" dependency chain something along these lines?\n\n1. system.img\n2. platform-bootclasspath and platform-systemserverclasspath\n3. A bunch of boot(systemserver?)classpath_fragment modules.\n4. A bunch of libs in the classpaths that should be dexpreopted.\n5. The paths to their dexpreopted outputs.\n\nI\u0027d expect #5 to become part of #1 through AndroidMk modules and the module dependency machinery in make. Apparently that\u0027s not the case, but can we make it closer to this path, to avoid fragility?\n\n+Paul who is the architect of the bootclasspath fragments.",
      "parentUuid": "f603bc0b_2bce10fd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "b23d4f5f7f34560eb4d284432ca250687a057ab7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3b9c064_51ecd48d",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_check.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-04T14:29:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Martin:\n\nThere are two dependency chains at different levels:\n\na) Soong-level module dependencies. Not interesting here, as they affect the order of generation of build rules, but not the actual build order or the set of things to be built. Nothing on this level depends on SS dexpreopt, it is just a piece Soong logic that runs when an SS jar is processed and generates Ninja build rules.\n\nb) Ninja-level file dependencies. On this level there _should_ be something that depends on SS dexpreopt files, but it\u0027s not necessarily the case now because we might have a dependency system.img -\u003e X, and the build rule for X might generate SS dexpreopt files as a byproduct. (I think this is the current situation and X is the .jar file, at least I couldn\u0027t track any other dependency in the Ninja files.)\n\nThe #5 you mentioned is on my level #b, #4 exists on both levels and #3 is purely on level #a, so I can\u0027t think about #1-#5 as one dependency chain.\n\nAFAIU Jiakai wants to add dependency system.img -\u003e SS dexpreopt to secure the implicit dependency that we have now. The test adds dependencies on dexpreopt for all PRODUCT_SYSTEM_SERVER_JARS + PRODUCT_APEX_SYSTEM_SERVER_JARS in a very easy-to-see-that-it-is-correct way and ensures that the complex logic in dexpreopt does the right thing.\n\nJiakai:\n\nI think this is not really a test, it should be a SingletonModule that generates makefile module that depends on dexpreopt files for all system server jars, and that makefile module should be added to dependencies of system.img (presumably via PRODUCT_PACKAGES). Then if we accidentally modify dexpreopt logic in Soong to omit some SS jar, this extra rule will fail the build.",
      "parentUuid": "f9f6b4a1_16e5f092",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "b23d4f5f7f34560eb4d284432ca250687a057ab7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1b5392e_e43bc995",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_check.go",
